Bounded filesystem protection smoke test
=======================================
Compile test-live.c against Android Bionic headers. Run only during authorized
rooted diagnostics after checking the four protected_* sysctl values. Creates a
new owned temporary directory, drops child UIDs/groups to test cross-owner link,
FIFO and regular-file protection in world/group-sticky directories, checks DAC
controls, then removes the fixture. Never reuses an existing directory. Does not
change sysctls, touch other files or provide an app-SELinux security test.
